<Layout title="Digital Ruble — Nikita Ostroukhov" description="Nikita Ostroukhov’s work on the Digital Ruble infrastructure.">
  <header><h1>Digital Ruble</h1><p class="subtitle">Took part in the development of the Digital Ruble infrastructure for EAEU.</p></header>
  <section>
    <p>
      From 2017 to 2019, I worked at TakeWing on an early implementation of a
      digital currency for the Eurasian Economic Union (EAEU), an initiative
      promoted by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sergey_Glazyev">Sergey Glazyev</a>, then adviser to the President of Russia on
      Eurasian integration.
    </p>
    <p>
      The project <a href="https://tass.ru/ekonomika/5229769">aimed</a> to create an autonomous cross-border settlement system
      for participating states, providing transaction confidentiality through
      zero-knowledge cryptography: the network could verify transactions without
      revealing who transferred funds to whom or in what amount. The broader
      goal was to establish a settlement infrastructure that could continue
      operating independently of external financial systems and remain resilient
      to foreign sanctions.
    </p>
    <p>
      The project was discontinued in 2019 for reasons unrelated to its technical development.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="contributions">
    <h2>Selected work</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="contribution-title">Ethereum / Geth</span><br />
      <span class="contribution-details">→ Worked on an independent fork of <a href="https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum">Geth</a> with a modified consensus mechanism and integrated system smart contracts providing protocol-level functionality, including support for zero-knowledge transactions.</span>
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="contribution-title">Smart Contracts</span><br />
      <span class="contribution-details">→ Designed system-level smart contracts implementing counterparty pre-filtering, consensus modifications, and other protocol features defining the currency’s behavior.</span>
    </p>
  </section>

